    <div class="col-12 col-md-9">
        <p class="lead">Keith Dunstan's earliest journalism appeared in Melbourne's evening paper, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Herald_(Melbourne)">The Herald</a>, from 1944.</p>
        <p>He joined The Herald and Weekly Times in 1946, and from 1949 to 1954 was its correspondent in New York and then London, writing the weekly 'Keith Dunstan's Hollywood' (later 'Film World') column and, in 1953, covering the Ashes tour of England. The articles held here are transcribed from scans in the National Library of Australia's Trove database.</p>
    </div>
